Lab 5: Jenkins Agents, Controllers, Dynamic Agents, and Docker Pipelines
--------------------
Areas Covered

What is Jenkins Agent, Its responsibilities.
What is Jenkins Controller and how it connects to agent.
Master and Agent/Node setup.
Run Jenkins pipeline on agent.
Dynamic Agent in Jenkins pipelines.
Docker pipeline plugin.
Cached dependencies.
Build Java/Python code on Dynamic agent.
-------------------------

Requirements

Jenkins Controller (master) running.
Docker installed on controller and a separate VM for static agent.
Docker Pipeline plugin.
Sample Python script in repo (e.g., pip install requests; python app.py).
--------------------------

Plan of Execution and Guidance

Master-Agent Setup:
Manage Jenkins > Manage Nodes > New Node > Permanent Agent > Name: static-agent.
Launch: Java Web Start on agent VM (download agent.jar, run java -jar agent.jar -jnlpUrl ... -secret ... -workDir /opt/jenkins).
Production Tip: Use SSH provisioning for agents; scale with Kubernetes plugin for 100+ nodes.
Run Pipeline on Agent:
In Jenkinsfile: agent { label 'static-agent' }.
-------------------------------

Dynamic Agents with Docker:
Install Docker plugin.
Jenkinsfile: agent { docker { image 'maven:3.9-jdk-17' } } for Java; docker { image 'python:3.11' } for Python.
Guidance: For caching, mount volumes: docker { image 'maven:3.9-jdk-17' args '-v /host/.m2:/root/.m2' }.
Build on Dynamic Agent:
Stages: Java Maven build; Python pip install -r requirements.txt && python -m unittest.
Production Tip: Use docker-workspace for persistent volumes; monitor agent resource usage via Metrics plugin.
------------------------------
Solution

Expected Outcome: Builds run on specified agents; Docker spins up ephemeral containers.
Jenkinsfile Snippet (Multi-Language):groovypipeline {
    agent none
    stages {
        stage('Java Build') {
            agent {
                docker {
                    image 'maven:3.9-jdk-17'
                    args '-v $HOME/.m2:/root/.m2'  // Cache deps
                }
            }
            steps { sh 'mvn clean package' }
        }
        stage('Python Build') {
            agent {
                label 'static-agent'  // Or docker 'python:3.11'
            }
            steps { sh 'pip install -r requirements.txt && python -m unittest' }
        }
    }
}
----------------------------------------------------------
Verification: Executor status shows agent usage; Docker logs: docker logs <container-id> confirm Maven/Python execution. Cache: Second run faster (no download).
